    "# Exploring production oracles (Chainlink):\n",
    "\n",
    "[Chainlink](https://chain.link/) is one of the most popular oracle providers on Ethereum. Let's take a high-level look at how the smart contracts for [the ETH-USD oracle on Chainlink](https://data.chain.link/ethereum/mainnet/crypto-usd/eth-usd) work for an example of how oracles can be implemented.\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Secured by Staking:** This is the total amount of LINK tokens locked as collateral by node operators to guarantee honest data reporting and economically penalize malicious behavior.\n",
    "* **Deviation threshold:** The oracle network will automatically push a new price to the blockchain if the off-chain price of ETH moves up or down by 0.5% or more.\n",
    "* **Heartbeat:** This is the maximum amount of time the network will wait before forcing an on-chain price update to prove the feed is alive, even if the price hasn't moved.\n",
    "* **Last update:** This indicates the exact time the oracle network most recently recorded a new ETH price onto the blockchain.\n",
    "* **Market cap:** This represents the total global value of the Ethereum network, calculated by multiplying the current ETH price by the circulating supply.\n",
    "* **Circulating supply:** This is the total number of ETH coins that currently exist and are actively available to trade in the public market.\n",
    "* **Volume (24hr):** This measures the total dollar value of Ethereum that has been bought and sold across all tracked exchanges over the past 24 hours.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "An end-to-end view of a price feed such as this consists of three types of contracts: \n",
    "1. A consumer contract \n",
    "2. A proxy contract \n",
    "3. An aggregator contract "
   ]
  },
  {
