    "### Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "**Execution Flow: Consumer -> Proxy -> Aggregator**\n",
    "\n",
    "* **1. Consumer Contract:** This is the smart contract you write (such as a DeFi lending protocol or decentralized exchange). It needs to fetch price data, but it doesn't need to understand how the underlying oracle network operates. It simply hardcodes the Proxy contract's address and sends data requests directly to it.\n",
    "* **2. Proxy Contract:** This acts as the stable, developer-facing \"middleman.\" It provides a persistent smart contract address that never changes. When a Consumer requests data, the Proxy seamlessly routes the call to the currently active Aggregator. This completely shields the Consumer contract from any underlying infrastructure upgrades or downtime.\n",
    "* **3. Aggregator Contract:** This is the actual \"data repository.\" Once Chainlink's decentralized nodes reach consensus off-chain, they write the latest asset prices directly into this contract. Whenever a system upgrade is required, Chainlink deploys a new Aggregator and updates the Proxy to point to it, while the previous Aggregator is preserved as a historical \"Phase.\"\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
