    "# Three Rounds of Reporting Test (All Honest, 1/3 Adversarial, 2/3 Adversarial)\n",
    "\n",
    "#### Assume this is a temperature oracle\n",
    "\n",
    "## Round 1: All Honest Reporting\n",
    "- All students in this class report the correct temperature value (you may check the current temperature by your phone or laptop).\n",
    "- Wait for required number of blocks (15 blocks) and call `processUpdate()`\n",
    "- Check the latest oracle value using `readValue()`\n",
    "\n",
    "You can report the value using the [Write Contract](https://sepolia.etherscan.io/address/0x5ACcd4dc94e91672E7aCd4D28D14a3A9ee131f7A#writeContract) tab on Etherscan. Call transaction `reportValue()` by providing 0.01 Sepolia ETH along with the value you wish to report\n",
    "\n",
    "Or you can use the following Python code snippet to report the value and process the update. \n",
    "\n",
    "Remember, in each round, every student can only report once. \n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "d27d9658",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Transaction sent with hash: 0xa96b2780374ac450d86c8e613af540c3fd286bfac61b57e972f1e29ed8efbcd9\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "current_temperature = 25 # Example temperature value to report\n",
    "contract_function = contract.functions.reportValue(current_temperature)\n",
    "trx = contract_function.build_transaction({\n",
    "    'from': wallet_public_address,\n",
    "    'value': contract.functions.REQUIRED_PAYMENT().call(), # Pay the required fee\n",
    "    'gas': 200000, # Set a gas limit\n",
    "    'gasPrice': web3.to_wei('10', 'gwei'), # Set a gas price\n",
    "    'nonce': web3.eth.get_transaction_count(wallet_public_address) # Get the current nonce\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "signed_txn = web3.eth.account.sign_transaction(trx, wallet_private_key)\n",
    "raw_transaction = signed_txn.rawTransaction if hasattr(signed_txn, 'rawTransaction') else signed_txn.raw_transaction\n",
    "\n",
    "trx_hash = web3.eth.send_raw_transaction(raw_transaction)\n",
    "print(f\"Transaction sent with hash: {web3.to_hex(trx_hash)}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "10ed18f7-89d4-4589-a3e6-59e03aab49f3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Remember, everyone who reports the median value during this round will split all the rewards, so it is in your interest to report a value as close as possible to what you think is the correct value. You can only make one report per round.\n",
    "\n",
    "Whenever at least `UPDATE_INTERVAL` blocks have passed since the last update, anyone can call `processUpdate()` to trigger the oracle update and rewards distribution. This example contract distributes Sepolia ETH as a reward, but you could easily imagine that the reward could be the protocol's token or something else similar instead.\n",
    "\n",
    "Try being the first to call `processUpdate()` to get the caller reward for free. \n",
    "\n",
    "*HINT: calling `readValue()` also tells you the last block the value was updated at. The variable `UPDATE_INTERVAL` defines the minimum number of blocks between intervals.*"
   ]
  },
